WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.314 --> 00:00:03.685
(screams)

00:00:03.685 --> 00:00:07.144
Whenever people tell us
Mariachi music is sacred

00:00:07.144 --> 00:00:09.362
and you can't change it or touch it,

00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:11.274
and believe me, there's a lot of people

00:00:11.274 --> 00:00:13.525
that are trying to convince us like

00:00:13.525 --> 00:00:16.994
what we're doing is like a musical sin,

00:00:16.994 --> 00:00:19.399
but in order to create
something new and beautiful

00:00:19.399 --> 00:00:21.720
you have to take risks, you
have to do something new,

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.888
or how would the something new

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:24.980
come about if you don't change it.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.063
(rock music playing)

00:00:29.951 --> 00:00:32.376
(classic rock tune)

00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:34.259
Metalachi is the first and only

00:00:34.259 --> 00:00:37.922
heavy metal Mariachi band in the world.

00:00:37.922 --> 00:00:40.642
We know what we're doing
when it comes to Mariachi.

00:00:40.642 --> 00:00:44.500
Before Metalachi everybody
spent years doing Mariachi,

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.923
or Charros, we did Mariachi for our life,

00:00:46.923 --> 00:00:48.672
that's how me made money.

00:00:48.672 --> 00:00:50.942
We use traditional Mariachi instruments.

00:00:50.942 --> 00:00:54.720
It's the same thing that you
would find in a Mariachi band.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.206
Doing what we do is not really that easy.

00:00:58.206 --> 00:01:00.588
To make a heavy metal
song into a Metalachi song,

00:01:00.588 --> 00:01:05.465
we have to invent rhythm, and
we basically create patterns.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.311
A lot of people don't see
it, they only hear like,

00:01:07.311 --> 00:01:10.006
"Ooh wow, that's a new pattern",
but the thing is, if we see

00:01:10.006 --> 00:01:13.338
people moving to it, then
we know we did a good job.

00:01:13.338 --> 00:01:16.171
Welcome to the stage, Metalachi!

00:01:18.721 --> 00:01:20.443
(Metalachi song)

00:01:20.443 --> 00:01:23.072
We cover a lot of different
types of bands, and everything

00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:25.731
like some you guys know, like Guns and Roses.

00:01:25.731 --> 00:01:29.386
♪ Welcome to the Jungle
We've got fun 'n' games ♪

00:01:29.386 --> 00:01:32.940
♪ Ai, ai, ai, come on! ♪

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.023
Ozzy Osborne.

00:01:35.892 --> 00:01:37.748
Hardcore stuff like Slayer,

00:01:37.748 --> 00:01:39.796
not so hardcore stuff
like Journey (scoffs),

00:01:39.796 --> 00:01:42.832
♪ She's just a small town girl ♪

00:01:42.832 --> 00:01:44.254
I mean, you name it, we do all of it.

00:01:44.254 --> 00:01:46.158
♪ Livin' in a lonely world ♪

00:01:46.158 --> 00:01:48.622
There's times where a
song translates very well,

00:01:48.622 --> 00:01:50.958
and we can pick it up in a couple hours,

00:01:50.958 --> 00:01:53.237
we can put something together
and it sounds really nice.

00:01:53.237 --> 00:01:55.820
(guitar intro)

00:01:59.037 --> 00:02:01.758
We've even traveled to
Mexico to go play over there,

00:02:01.758 --> 00:02:03.541
and not really knowing
how they would accept it,

00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:06.076
because there's a lot of people
that are very traditional,

00:02:06.076 --> 00:02:08.116
you know, they love it
because Mariachi music

00:02:08.116 --> 00:02:10.908
is about life, it's about beauty.

00:02:10.908 --> 00:02:12.255
So it's like the metal music and they’re

00:02:12.255 --> 00:02:14.476
actually singing about the same stuff.

00:02:14.476 --> 00:02:18.059
They just do it in
their own different way.

00:02:20.222 --> 00:02:21.725
By integrating the two things, we are

00:02:21.725 --> 00:02:25.415
showing Mariachi people this
music is also beautiful.

00:02:25.415 --> 00:02:26.979
But originally, heavy metal music is that

00:02:26.979 --> 00:02:29.470
your music can be
interpreted in a different way, you know?

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.206
So, I think, we like that message
that's being sent out.

00:02:32.206 --> 00:02:35.539
(touching violin solo)

